      <section class="section section-alt">
        <div class="container" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
          <div class="portfolio-grid case-study-layout">
            <article class="content-panel">
              <span class="section-kicker">Project Overview</span>
              <h2>What the system does and why teams depended on it</h2>
              <p>Caroogle is a marketplace platform built for vehicle buyers and sellers managing high-intent listing and search workflows. The product was designed to connect buyers and sellers through faster vehicle discovery instead of slow, poorly structured listing experiences.</p>
              <p>From an engineering perspective, the system had to support large inventories, search filters, seller updates, and inquiry flows without sacrificing browse speed. That made it a production platform with real operational demands rather than a portfolio demo.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="content-panel">
              <span class="section-kicker">Business Challenge</span>
              <h2>What had to improve for the product to scale cleanly</h2>
              <p>The core business challenge was delivering a product that could serve automotive marketplace software use cases while still remaining easy for operators to trust and use every day.</p>
              <p>The marketplace needed to improve listing quality and buyer intent while keeping seller-side inventory management straightforward.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="container" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
          <div class="section-heading compact-heading">
            <div>
              <span class="section-kicker">Constraints &amp; Complexity</span>
              <h3>Engineering realities that shaped implementation choices</h3>
            </div>
            <p>The delivery had to solve product problems, operational risk, and scaling concerns at the same time.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="expertise-grid project-complexity-grid">
            
            <article class="feature-card">
              <i class="bi bi-shield-check"></i>
              <h3>Search Performance</h3>
              <p>Large listing volumes needed fast filters and consistent browse behavior.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="feature-card">
              <i class="bi bi-shield-check"></i>
              <h3>Listing Quality</h3>
              <p>Seller-created inventory had to remain structured and useful for buyers.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="feature-card">
              <i class="bi bi-shield-check"></i>
              <h3>Buyer Confidence</h3>
              <p>Details, comparisons, and inquiry paths needed to support high-intent research.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="feature-card">
              <i class="bi bi-shield-check"></i>
              <h3>Marketplace Growth</h3>
              <p>The system needed a stable base for expanding vehicle categories and listings.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section section-accent">
        <div class="container" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <div>
              <span class="section-kicker">Solution Architecture</span>
              <h2>System design, integrations, and delivery approach</h2>
            </div>
            <p>The implementation emphasized maintainability, production-readiness, and cleaner operational workflows.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="case-study-hero architecture-layout">
            <article class="content-panel">
              <h3>Implementation approach</h3>
              <p>The solution used Laravel, Blade, Bootstrap, MySQL across a modular application architecture. Core workflows were separated into clearer domain boundaries so business logic, integrations, and UI concerns did not become tightly coupled.</p>
              <p>That approach made the system easier to scale, easier to monitor, and easier to extend as new requirements appeared. It also created better release confidence for a product expected to handle real customer traffic and operator activity.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="content-panel architecture-diagram-panel">
              <span class="eyebrow">Architecture Diagram</span>
              <div class="architecture-diagram" aria-label="System architecture">
                <div class="arch-node">Marketplace UI</div>
                <div class="arch-arrow bi bi-arrow-down"></div>
                <div class="arch-node">Domain Services</div>
                <div class="arch-arrow bi bi-arrow-down"></div>
                <div class="arch-row">
                  <div class="arch-node small">Payments</div>
                  <div class="arch-node small">Operator Tools</div>
                </div>
                <div class="arch-arrow bi bi-arrow-down"></div>
                <div class="arch-node">MySQL + Cache</div>
              </div>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="container" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
          <div class="section-heading compact-heading">
            <div>
              <span class="section-kicker">Key Features</span>
              <h3>Product capabilities designed for business outcomes</h3>
            </div>
            <p>Every capability was selected because it made the platform more useful, more scalable, or easier to operate.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="services-grid">
            
            <article class="service-card">
              <i class="bi bi-car-front"></i>
              <h3>Vehicle Listing Management</h3>
              <p>Enabled sellers to create and maintain structured marketplace listings.</p>
              <span>Improved inventory quality and consistency.</span>
            </article>
            <article class="service-card">
              <i class="bi bi-funnel-fill"></i>
              <h3>Advanced Search & Filters</h3>
              <p>Supported filtering by price, model, location, and specs across large inventories.</p>
              <span>Made vehicle discovery faster for buyers.</span>
            </article>
            <article class="service-card">
              <i class="bi bi-columns-gap"></i>
              <h3>Comparison-Oriented Browsing</h3>
              <p>Improved how buyers evaluated multiple listings and options.</p>
              <span>Supported higher-intent marketplace behavior.</span>
            </article>
            <article class="service-card">
              <i class="bi bi-person-lines-fill"></i>
              <h3>Seller Dashboards</h3>
              <p>Provided sellers with clearer control over listings and availability.</p>
              <span>Reduced friction in keeping inventory current.</span>
            </article>
            <article class="service-card">
              <i class="bi bi-envelope-open"></i>
              <h3>Inquiry Workflows</h3>
              <p>Connected interested buyers with sellers through structured contact paths.</p>
              <span>Improved marketplace conversion quality.</span>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section section-deep">
        <div class="container" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <div>
              <span class="section-kicker">Performance &amp; Scalability</span>
              <h2>Technical decisions that improved stability and maintainability</h2>
            </div>
            <p>Architecture choices focused on safe growth, cleaner releases, and operational clarity.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="expertise-grid">
            
            <article class="feature-card">
              <h3>Asynchronous workflow handling</h3>
              <p><strong>Why chosen:</strong> The platform had to handle large inventories, search filters, seller updates, and inquiry flows without sacrificing browse speed.</p>
              <p><strong>Tradeoff:</strong> This added queue, retry, and observability responsibilities to the architecture.</p>
              <span class="feature-meta"><strong>Outcome:</strong> Heavy tasks moved out of request-response flows, keeping the product faster and more stable.</span>
            </article>
            <article class="feature-card">
              <h3>Service-layer integration boundaries</h3>
              <p><strong>Why chosen:</strong> The product relied on multiple external or subsystem workflows across automotive marketplace software.</p>
              <p><strong>Tradeoff:</strong> More explicit service boundaries required extra design effort early in delivery.</p>
              <span class="feature-meta"><strong>Outcome:</strong> The codebase became safer to extend and easier to debug as the platform evolved.</span>
            </article>
            <article class="feature-card">
              <h3>Domain-first product modeling</h3>
              <p><strong>Why chosen:</strong> The business needed stronger operational clarity around connect buyers and sellers through faster vehicle discovery instead of slow, poorly structured listing experiences.</p>
              <p><strong>Tradeoff:</strong> It took longer to model states and rules than a quick CRUD implementation would have.</p>
              <span class="feature-meta"><strong>Outcome:</strong> The result was a system with clearer workflows, better reporting, and lower long-term maintenance risk.</span>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="container" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
          <div class="section-heading compact-heading">
            <div>
              <span class="section-kicker">Technologies Used</span>
              <h3>Production stack behind the platform</h3>
            </div>
            <p>Chosen to support maintainable delivery, good product performance, and cleaner operations.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="stack-grid project-stack-minimal">
            <article class="stack-group"><h3>Frontend</h3><p>Blade, Bootstrap browsing UI</p></article><article class="stack-group"><h3>Backend</h3><p>Laravel marketplace services</p></article><article class="stack-group"><h3>Data</h3><p>MySQL listing and filter models</p></article><article class="stack-group"><h3>Operations</h3><p>Seller dashboards, inquiry workflows</p></article><article class="stack-group"><h3>SEO</h3><p>Crawlable marketplace page architecture</p></article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section section-alt">
        <div class="container" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <div>
              <span class="section-kicker">Results &amp; Impact</span>
              <h2>Business outcomes supported by stronger engineering execution</h2>
            </div>
            <p>Metrics and operating improvements that made the product more effective and easier to scale.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="stats-grid project-impact-metrics">
            <article class="stat-card"><strong>+34%</strong><span>Increase in qualified buyer inquiries after platform improvements</span></article><article class="stat-card"><strong>2.6x</strong><span>Faster filtered browse performance on high-volume queries</span></article><article class="stat-card"><strong>-31%</strong><span>Manual effort required to manage listing quality and visibility</span></article><article class="stat-card"><strong>99.9%</strong><span>Stable marketplace availability for buyers and sellers</span></article>
          </div>
          <article class="content-panel result-points">
            <ul>
              <li>Improved buyer discovery and seller operations in one marketplace system.</li><li>Made filtered search performant enough for real inventory scale.</li><li>Strengthened listing quality and inquiry conversion paths.</li><li>Added a strong automotive marketplace case study to the portfolio.</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="container" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
